iseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()","title":"hamiltonianPath()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, extending through each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindHamiltonianPath"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}]},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/isEulerian":{"type":"topic","title":"isEulerian","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether some closed trail uses every edge exactly once: every degree is even (a self-loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counts 2) and the vertices with edges are connected. Isolated vertices are ignored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(igraph’s and JGraphT’s rule; NetworkX counts them), and an edgeless graph, the empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","tex